message:
[UPDATE] Improved execution flow and input handling in SMG setup scripts

- Updated `config_smg.ksh` to allow function execution with arbitrary arguments (e.g., `copy_ncep_inputs YYYYMMDDHH`);
- Modified `execute_function` to pass all parameters beyond the first one to the called function;
- Enhanced documentation in `config_smg.ksh` and `smg_setup.sh` with ProTex-style comments;
- Added robust input parsing and progress output for `copy_ncep_inputs`;
- Minor formatting and shell style improvements (quoting, spacing, echo style).

Tested on EGEON with command:
  ./config_smg.ksh copy_ncep_inputs 2025070100
